From: Luke Howard <lukeh@padl.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bootstrap: install directory-form swiftmodules under the native engine

With --build-system native, SwiftPM 6.4 writes swiftmodule/swiftdoc files as
FLAT FILES in a Modules/ subdirectory of the bin path, while shared libraries
stay flat in the bin path itself:

    <bin_dir>/libPackageDescription.so
    <bin_dir>/Modules/PackageDescription.swiftmodule

Utilities/bootstrap's install_dylib() looks for the swiftmodule flat in
bin_dir, so `bootstrap install` dies with FileNotFoundError -- and installing
the flat file as-is is not enough either: the swiftbuild engine and the
swift.org toolchain bundles both ship DIRECTORY-form modules
(Foo.swiftmodule/<module-triple>.swiftmodule). A toolchain whose module shape
differs from the prebuilt bundles breaks OpenEmbedded sysroot staging when a
build switches between the two toolchain providers: the departing component's
file removal leaves an empty Foo.swiftmodule/ directory behind, and staging
the incoming flat file onto that path fails with FileExistsError.

Normalise on install: pick the flat files up from Modules/ and install them
directory-form, named by the module triple Utilities/bootstrap already has in
args.target_info. Layouts without a flat Modules/ copy (swiftbuild) install
unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround for an upstream bug, not yet reported]
---
--- a/Utilities/bootstrap
+++ b/Utilities/bootstrap
@@ -521,9 +521,30 @@
     # Install the dynamic library itself.
     install_binary(args, g_shared_lib_prefix + library_name + g_shared_lib_suffix, install_dir, bin_dir)
 
+    # The native build system emits swiftmodules as flat files in a Modules/
+    # subdirectory of the bin path, while the swiftbuild engine (and the
+    # swift.org toolchain bundles) use directory-form modules
+    # (Foo.swiftmodule/<module-triple>.swiftmodule). Normalise to
+    # directory-form on install so a toolchain built with either engine has
+    # the same on-disk shape -- consumers (and OE's sysroot staging, which
+    # cannot swap a directory for a file in place) depend on it.
+    module_bin_dir = os.path.join(bin_dir, "Modules")
+    module_triple = args.target_info["target"]["moduleTriple"]
+
     # Install the swiftmodule/swiftinterface and swiftdoc files for all the modules.
     for module in module_names:
-        install_binary(args, module + ".swiftmodule", install_dir, bin_dir, ignored_patterns=['Project'])
+        flat = os.path.join(module_bin_dir, module + ".swiftmodule")
+        if not os.path.exists(flat):
+            # Not a flat-module layout: install whatever bin_dir has, as-is.
+            install_binary(args, module + ".swiftmodule", install_dir, bin_dir, ignored_patterns=['Project'])
+            continue
+        dest = os.path.join(install_dir, module + ".swiftmodule")
+        mkdir_p(dest)
+        for ext in [".swiftmodule", ".swiftdoc", ".swiftinterface"]:
+            src = os.path.join(module_bin_dir, module + ext)
+            if os.path.exists(src):
+                logging.info("Installing %s into %s", src, dest)
+                shutil.copy2(src, os.path.join(dest, module_triple + ext))
 
 # Helper function that installs a single built artifact to a particular directory. The source may be either a file or a directory.
 @log_entry_exit
